          "author": "J Oviedo",
          "authorPhoto": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocK0nssJAZylWS9I-IUeGC39DxeKafNql26X-qWNyD3NJsGpdNI=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
          "rating": 1,
          "text": "I went to LIV Miami for Pedro Sampaio's concert, and honestly, the experience was extremely disappointing. It was surprising to see an artist like Pedro Sampaio, who is known for supporting the LGBTQ+ community, performing at a venue that felt anything but welcoming.\n\nA friend of mine and his group had VIP tickets and access to a table area, but they were denied entry because the group consisted entirely of men. Staff told them they would only be allowed in if they committed to spending at least $2,000 on table service, which felt completely unreasonable and excessive. When they declined, they were simply not allowed to enter.\n\nInside the venue, the security staff made the experience even worse. They constantly pushed and monitored people whenever someone was entering or leaving an area, often speaking in a rude and aggressive manner and telling guests to move out of the way as if they were an inconvenience. There was very little professionalism or respect shown toward attendees.\n\nWhat made the situation even more frustrating was that security seemed to ignore other guests who were openly smoking marijuana and blowing smoke into the crowd, creating discomfort for those around them.\n\nOverall, this was one of the least welcoming venues I have ever visited. The atmosphere felt hostile, especially toward groups of men, and it certainly did not feel inclusive. I would never return, even for a regular party. If an artist I like performs at LIV again, I would seriously consider skipping the event rather than risk another experience like this.",
